# Hearth nightly backup.
#
# PATH is set explicitly because cron's default is /usr/bin:/bin, which does
# NOT include /usr/local/bin -- where rclone lives. Without this line backup.sh
# dies on "rclone: command not found". The apt rclone was removed precisely so
# that failure is loud rather than a silent downgrade to a 2022 client.
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# 19:17 UTC == 03:17 Asia/Singapore. The conversion is done HERE, by hand,
# because Ubuntu's cron (vixie 3.0pl1) IGNORES CRON_TZ -- proven on this box on
# 2026-08-16 by scheduling a probe in Singapore time under CRON_TZ and watching
# it not fire. An earlier version of this file set CRON_TZ and claimed the
# schedule read as local time; it did not, and the backup would have run at
# 11:17 in the morning instead.
#
# Singapore observes no daylight saving, so this fixed UTC time always means
# 03:17 locally. Any timezone that DOES observe DST would drift by an hour
# twice a year and would need a different approach.
17 19 * * * set -a; . /home/deploy/hearth-backup.env; set +a; /home/deploy/Household/deploy/backup.sh >> /home/deploy/hearth-backup.log 2>&1
